# Use the local myoracle MCP server

Operational work goes through the local MCP server at `oracle_single/myoracle_mcp/server.py`. That includes Oracle queries, saved connections, alert logs, SSH on saved hosts, backups, and related checks.

- Discover and call the existing `@mcp.tool()` functions. Do not open a saved connection from a one-off script, `sqlplus`, or a private import of `server.py`.
- If no tool can perform the task, add that tool before doing the work another way, then finish the original task by calling the new tool. Use the `add-myoracle-tool` skill for the full workflow (module under `oracle_single/myoracle_mcp/`, one `@mcp.tool()` in `server.py`, README entry, test in `test_server.py` when it can run without a live database).